<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0"><head><title>Living character sheet</title></head><body>
<outline text="# Living character sheet">
  <outline text="A solo-play character whose numbers compute themselves. The stats are variables, the derived rows read those variables, the pack total adds up its own contents, and the encumbrance check flags overload the moment you carry too much. Every {…} is a live pill: click one to roll or re-run it. See character-sheet.md for the walkthrough."/>
  <outline text="## Kestrel Vane, hedge-scout">
    <outline text="A wary tracker who works the forest edge. Change a number below and watch the rows that depend on it move."/>
    <outline text="## Core stats (edit these)">
      <outline text="Level: {level := 3}"/>
      <outline text="Might (raw): {might := 2}"/>
      <outline text="Grace (raw): {grace := 3}"/>
      <outline text="Wits (raw): {wits := 1}"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="## Derived numbers (these compute themselves)">
      <outline text="Hit points, eight per level: {= level * 8}"/>
      <outline text="Defense, ten plus grace: {= 10 + grace}"/>
      <outline text="Carry limit (a soft cap of ten load): {= 10}"/>
      <outline text="Proficiency, half your level rounded up: {= ceil(level / 2)}"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="## Rolls that read the sheet">
      <outline text="Attack (2d6 plus might): {2d6+might}"/>
      <outline text="Sneak (2d6 plus grace): {2d6+grace}"/>
      <outline text="Study a clue (2d6 plus wits): {2d6+wits}"/>
      <outline text="Save under pressure (2d6, beat 8 plus level scaling): {2d6} vs {= 8 + level}"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="## Pack (the total adds itself, load ten or under)">
      <outline text="Carried load, carrying {= sum(weight)} of 10" _props="[{&quot;key&quot;:&quot;check&quot;,&quot;val&quot;:&quot;sum(weight) &lt;= 10&quot;}]">
        <outline text="Short bow {prop weight: 2}"/>
        <outline text="Quiver, twenty arrows {prop weight: 1}"/>
        <outline text="Hunting knife {prop weight: 1}"/>
        <outline text="Leather jerkin {prop weight: 3}"/>
        <outline text="Bedroll and cloak {prop weight: 2}"/>
        <outline text="Rations, three days {prop weight: 1}"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Add one more heavy item to see the check flip. Copy this into the pack: Iron cook pot `{prop weight: 2}`. The sum climbs to twelve and the Carried load chip goes red."/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="## Scene: a name for the tracks">
      <outline text="You cut the trail of {a wounded stag | a lone rider | something with too many feet}. Which way does it lead? {deeper in | back toward the road | in a slow circle}."/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## How to run it">
    <outline text="Change a stat and watch the sheet move. Click Level above, set it to 5, and the hit points row ({= level * 8}) jumps to forty on its own. The attack roll ({2d6+might}) reads Might the same way, so raising a raw stat raises every row that uses it."/>
    <outline text="Watch the check catch a problem. The Carried load chip runs `sum(weight)` over the pack items directly under it and passes while the total is ten or under. Add the cook pot line (or bump any weight up), the total on the Carried load point crosses ten, and the chip turns red. Take something out and it clears. Search is:failing to find every check that is currently red across the whole document."/>
    <outline text="Nothing here is new syntax. Stats are variables (name colon-equals value), derived rows are math that reads them (equals then an expression), the pack total is a child rollup (`{= sum(weight)}` on the Carried load point itself, whose child items each carry a weight property), and the encumbrance rule is a check on the Carried load point (add one from its bullet menu, or type /check, with the test `sum(weight) &lt;= 10`). See character-sheet.md."/>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body></opml>
